      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the measures of the interior angles of the triangle, we start by letting the measures of the angles be \\(5x\\), \\(6x\\), and \\(7x\\). Since the sum of the interior angles of a triangle is always \\(180^\\circ\\), we can write the equation:\n\n\\[5x + 6x + 7x = 180^\\circ\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[18x = 180^\\circ\\]\n\nTo find \\(x\\), we divide both sides of the equation by 18:\n\n\\[x = \\frac{180^\\circ}{18} = 10^\\circ\\]\n\nNow, we can find the measures of the individual angles by substituting \\(x = 10^\\circ\\) back into the expressions for the angles:\n\n\\[5x = 5 \\times 10^\\circ = 50^\\circ\\]\n\\[6x = 6 \\times 10^\\circ = 60^\\circ\\]\n\\[7x = 7 \\times 10^\\circ = 70^\\circ\\]\n\nThe smallest interior angle is \\(50^\\circ\\). Therefore, the measure of the smallest interior angle is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{50}\\]",
